{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - User - Authentication - Okta Invalid Credential Attempts by Source [table]",
	"Description": "Groups sign-in attempts Okta rejected for invalid credentials by source address, with the account count alongside. This is the narrower cousin of the brute force detection: it keys on Okta's INVALID_CREDENTIALS outcome reason rather than any failure, so it excludes policy denials and lockouts and shows only attempts where the password itself was wrong.\n\nThreshold: 10 or more invalid credential attempts from one address. Edit the eval near the end of the query to tune it.\n\nThis detection uses stats, so it renders as a table rather than shipping raw entries.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/event-types/\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/api/openapi/okta-management/management/tag/SystemLog/\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
	"GUID": "ffbec52d-492c-5ec5-96e8-ebcf07ec6e2d",
	"SearchReference": "0eeb706e-23c8-5fac-9358-5ee4a2227d2f"
}